{#
    The bar. One of them, for every kind of page.

    Its parts are configuration — the mark, the sections, the footer's sibling
    — so a manual page and a landing page carry the same one and a reader
    never has to work out which site they are on.
#}
<header class="sds-bar">
    {#- The mobile menu: one button that opens the rail the layout gives this
        id to. It adds behaviour and takes none away — without JavaScript there
        is no button, and the rail is where it always was. -#}
    <sds-menu for="page-rail" label="Pages"></sds-menu>
    {% include "structure/brand.html.twig" %}
    {% include "structure/navigation.html.twig" %}
    <div class="sds-bar__end">
        <sds-search index="{{ root }}_search.json" label="Search the documentation"></sds-search>
        <sds-theme key="soul-theme"></sds-theme>
    </div>
</header>
